&lt;h3&gt;About YLD:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to help our clients keep moving forward. We work with them to build the skills and capabilities they need to stay ahead of the competition, and we know our success only happens when they succeed. We’re a team of curious, talented people, and we’re committed to making YLD a place where great people want to work, grow, and stay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a remote-first consultancy specialising in software engineering, product design, and data. Our teams are based across London, Lisbon, and Porto, and we create digital solutions that continue to deliver value long after our work is done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the role:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Platform Software Engineer at YLD, you&#39;ll be part of a client team, owning cloud access and identity management along with a large part of their infrastructure-as-code. Day to day, that means controlling who and what can do what across their cloud estate, and standing up the newer tooling that sits alongside it. It&#39;s shared infrastructure that many teams depend on, so much of the role is careful change management, governance, and unblocking others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Skills:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, hands-on AWS experience, particularly IAM, IAM Identity Center / SSO, and AWS Organizations (essential)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Terraform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running shared, high-blast-radius infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitHub Actions for CI/CD, including OIDC federation to cloud providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Datadog, CloudWatch, or similar tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some Python or JavaScript for scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-cloud experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong focus on clean engineering practices, including testing and reliability;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools to augment your work, applying sound judgement to adopt emerging technologies where they genuinely add value and increase your impact as an engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get in return:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to work with a forward-thinking, ethical, and fun group of people and to develop and grow your skills in a fast-moving business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our typical recruitment process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1st Interview with a Talent Partner (30/45 mins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Interview with our Senior Developers (1h30)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final chat with our Client Partner (30/45 mins)&lt;/li&gt

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; color: #662d91;&quot;&gt;Teamwork makes the stream work.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;font-family: GothamBold,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roku is changing how the world watches TV&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roku is the #1 TV streaming platform in the U.S., Canada, and Mexico, and we&#39;ve set our sights on powering every television in the world. Roku pioneered streaming to the TV. Our mission is to be the TV streaming platform that connects the entire TV ecosystem. We connect consumers to the content they love, enable content publishers to build and monetize large audiences, and provide advertisers unique capabilities to engage consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From your first day at Roku, you&#39;ll make a valuable - and valued - contribution. We&#39;re a fast-growing public company where no one is a bystander. We offer you the opportunity to delight millions of TV streamers around the world while gaining meaningful experience across a variety of disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-6 mb-2 font-semibold text-xl&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;heading-3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;font-semibold&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;What does the team work on?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-200 my-2.5 last:mb-0 first:mt-0 &quot;&gt;The Roku Enterprise Engineering team is at the forefront of building a robust, integrated, and scalable platform that powers critical business processes across the organisation. As a cornerstone of Roku&#39;s corporate strategy, this team is instrumental in automating workflows across all Business Systems, including Supply Chain, Finance, Sales Operations, and Human Resources. By challenging traditional approaches to workflow automation, the team leverages cutting-edge engineering practices and API-driven design to streamline internal processes, boost efficiency, and deliver innovative solutions. The team&#39;s expertise spans a wide range of technologies, including Java and Python-based MicroServices, AWS/GCP cloud backend systems, Big Data technologies like Hive and Spark, and modern web applications. With a globally distributed presence across the US, India, and Europe, the team thrives on collaboration, bringing together diverse perspectives to solve complex challenges. At the heart of their success is a shared commitment to technical excellence, creativity, a strong sense of ownership, and a collaborative spirit that drives impactful results for Roku&#39;s business operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;mt-6 mb-2 font-semibold text-xl&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;heading-3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;font-semibold&quot; data-streamdown=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;What is the role?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-neutral-900 dark:text-ne

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The senior Full-Stack Engineer will be an integral part of our Engineering teams in EMEA.This role is based remotely as a full-time employee in the UK, Ireland, Estonia, the Netherlands, Sweden and Israel. We are also open to contractors in Eastern Europe and Portugal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;DoiT is a global technology company that works with cloud-driven organizations to leverage the cloud to drive business growth and innovation. We combine data, technology, and human expertise to ensure our customers operate in a well-architected and scalable state - from planning to production.&lt;br&gt;Delivering DoiT Cloud Intelligence, the only solution that integrates advanced technology with human intelligence, we help our customers solve complex multicloud problems and drive efficiency.&lt;br&gt;With decades of multicloud experience, we have specializations in Kubernetes, GenAI, CloudOps, and more. An award-winning strategic partner of AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure, we work alongside more than 4,000 customers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;AI is the fastest-growing line on our customers&#39; cloud bills - and the hardest one to see. Model APIs, managed inference, GPUs, and a growing fleet of agentic coding tools each report spend differently, and most teams still can&#39;t answer the basic questions: what are we spending, on which workloads, for which teams, and is it worth it. Our AI cost visibility product, part of DoiT Cloud Intelligence, exists to answer them.&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Senior Full-Stack Engineer into our R&amp;amp;D team to own this product end-to-end - from the Go services that ingest and model AI spend, through the APIs that expose it, to the React interfaces where FinOps practitioners and platform engineers make decisions. This is a young product in a category being defined right now. You&#39;ll shape how it works, not just implement someone else&#39;s spec, and there is a short line from your work to what customers see.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll work AI-augmented from day one. We expect you to use AI across your whole workflow - not as an occasional autocomplete - and to have real opinions about where it earns its place and where it doesn&#39;t.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning features end-to-end. This is the core of the role. Take a problem from understanding the customer&#39;s pain, through design and implementation, to release, monitoring and iteration. You define what done looks like and you own the outcome - reliability, user experience and measurable impact included. Propose the work you think should happen; you&#39;re not here to wait for a spec.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowing the product and the domain. Understand how AI spend actually works - token and model pricing, inference

