&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Moniepoint Inc. is Africa’s all-in-one financial platform, helping 20 million businesses and individuals access seamless payments, banking, credit, cross-border, and business management tools each month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Nigeria’s largest merchant acquirer, we power most of the country’s point-of-sale (POS) transactions. Through our subsidiaries, Moniepoint Inc. processes over $250 billion in digital payment transaction value annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why United Kingdom&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UK is home to our headquarters where more than 70 team members are based. Our London office is located at Sea Containers, just by London Bridge - this is also where a significant number of our most senior leaders sit, which makes it a natural base for a Head of Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, now we are looking for our Head of Engineering, Supply Chain to join us in the UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;POS Hardware and Device Platforms owns the software behind the physical side of Moniepoint&#39;s business: the systems that track, move, maintain and account for millions of POS terminals in the field. That covers inventory and warehouse management, logistics and distribution, repair and maintenance workflows, and the operational tooling the business runs on day to day. It is a backend and distributed systems challenge at real scale - making operational data about millions of physical devices visible, trustworthy and consistent across every market we operate in. It is not a hardware engineering role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of Engineering, POS Supply Chain, oversees that software estate and is vital as Moniepoint expands internationally and scales device operations globally. The position involves leading the technical strategy for the domain and managing a large engineering organisation in a remote, distributed environment. As Head of Engineering, Supply Chain, your responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the technical strategy and architecture for inventory and logistics tools and repair management software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading an engineering organisation of approximately 25 engineers, including managers, QA, SRE and Data Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving&amp;nbsp;platformisation of inventory and supply chain systems so operational data is visible, trustworthy and consistent across millions of terminals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridging the gap between operational practice and software systems by building operationally disciplined solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining architecture standards, engineering processes and quality metrics across squads to ensure reliability and data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with business and operational stakeholders to translate operational requirements into engineering solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
